<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vorma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vorma is a short river in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> that drains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-mjosa">Lake Mjøsa</a> south past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsvoll">Eidsvoll</a> to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glomma">Glomma</a> at Nes in Romerike. Its valley, among the most fertile farmland in Norway, has been densely settled since prehistoric times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vorma.jpg" alt="Vorma" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vorma_in_Norway.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
